# Project 00 — Homelab Hardware Planning & Infrastructure Design

## 1. Project Overview

Hello !! Welcome to my homelab project blueprint. The idea of this project came from my I.T/Cybersecurity background and enjoying it as a hobby.

I designed and assembled a three-node homelab to develop practical skills in Linux system administration, networking, virtualization, cybersecurity, and infrastructure automation.

My primary objective is to gain hands-on experience with technologies used in professional IT environments while building a platform that can also host personal services.

The infrastructure is designed to support:

- Linux administration and RHCSA training
- Network configuration, troubleshooting, and packet analysis
- Virtualization using Proxmox VE
- Cybersecurity monitoring and network segmentation
- Bash scripting and infrastructure automation
- Dedicated game servers
- Self-hosted media and cloud services

A major consideration during the planning process was balancing hardware cost, resource requirements, power consumption, expandability, and the ability to operate the environment continuously.

